    "extraction_notes": [
      "The supplied PDF SHA-256 is fbe2d17e4ed91161bcc8a52a51936a45844d1e68019838832162a1e564dc4340.",
      "The 25 °C transfer curve was digitized from p. 3 Figure 2 at VDS = 5 V. The separate 125 °C curve is present in the figure but omitted from the structured curve set because the extraction target is the 25 °C curve.",
      "The output curves were digitized from p. 3 Figure 1 for VGS = 3.5 V, 4.0 V, 4.5 V, 5.0 V, and 10.0 V. Datasheet Note E states pulses <300 µs and duty cycle 0.5% maximum.",
      "The Ciss, Coss, and Crss traces were digitized from p. 4 Figure 8. The electrical-characteristics table gives the associated bias as VGS = 0 V, VDS = 20 V, and f = 1 MHz.",
      "RDS(ON) publishes typical and maximum values at VGS = 10 V, ID = 20 A for TJ = 25 °C and 125 °C, plus VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 15 A at TJ = 25 °C. No minimum RDS(ON) values are published.",
      "The VSD table value is typical 0.7 V and maximum 1.0 V at IS = 1 A, VGS = 0 V. Figure 6 additionally shows typical body-diode curves at 25 °C and 125 °C; the structured body_diode value uses the typical table value.",
      "Published values not representable by the strict schema include IDSS maximum 1 µA at VDS = 40 V, VGS = 0 V, TJ = 25 °C and 5 µA at TJ = 55 °C; Rg typical 3.5 ohm and maximum 5 ohm at VGS = 0 V, VDS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz; Qg(10V) typical 27 nC and maximum 33 nC; Qg(4.5V) typical 14 nC and maximum 17 nC; Qgs typical 5 nC and maximum 6 nC; Qgd typical 6 nC and maximum 9 nC, with gate-charge conditions VGS = 10 V, VDS = 20 V, ID = 20 A; and trr typical 29 ns, maximum 38 ns plus Qrr typical 26 nC, maximum 34 nC at IF = 20 A, di/dt = 100 A/µs.",
      "Thermal resistance values not representable by the strict schema are RθJC typical 2.4 °C/W, maximum 3 °C/W, RθJA typical 18 °C/W and maximum 22 °C/W for t ≤ 10 s, and RθJA typical 44 °C/W and maximum 55 °C/W steady-state."
    ],
